{"action":"created","issue":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sunpy/sunpy/issues/7279","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sunpy/sunpy","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sunpy/sunpy/issues/7279/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sunpy/sunpy/issues/7279/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sunpy/sunpy/issues/7279/events","html_url":"https://github.com/sunpy/sunpy/issues/7279","id":1970476825,"node_id":"I_kwDOACEKh851cxcZ","number":7279,"title":"Change `Fido.fetch()` to raise an error if one or more files failed to download","user":{"login":"ayshih","id":991759,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk5MTc1OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/991759?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ayshih","html_url":"https://github.com/ayshih","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ayshih/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ayshih/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ayshih/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ayshih/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ayshih/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ayshih/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ayshih/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ayshih/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ayshih/received_events","type":"User","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":7928469,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3OTI4NDY5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sunpy/sunpy/labels/Feature%20Request","name":"Feature Request","color":"009800","default":false,"description":"New feature wanted!"},{"id":123240217,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxMjMyNDAyMTc=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sunpy/sunpy/labels/net","name":"net","color":"c7def8","default":false,"description":"Affects the net submodule"}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignee":null,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2023-10-31T13:28:42Z","updated_at":"2023-10-31T17:37:20Z","closed_at":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","active_lock_reason":null,"body":"Currently, `Fido.fetch()` does not interrupt execution with an error if one or more files failed to download.  This results in confusing behavior for *non-interactive* scripts, such as our gallery examples, where the script fails later down because the code then tries to work with non-existent filenames.  I think that `Fido.fetch()` should raise an error, after all downloads have been attempted, so the script does not keep executing past the `fetch()` call.  I suspect that in the majority of cases, the script will want all the files to have been successfully downloaded before continuing.  In the minority of cases where the script would want to keep going even with failed downloads, the `fetch()` call can simply be wrapped in a `try...except` block.

